              "Reviewed the guide and completed an opening S05 experiment.\n\nA parity-based Taylor evaluator gives narrower complete enclosures for \\(\\Phi,\\Phi',\\Phi''\\). On \\([0,1/1024]\\), the radius improvements are approximately **894×, 7.3×, and 2,395×**, verified at 192 and 256 bits with full tails and remainder bounds.\n\nSaved the [derivation](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/05_covariant_theta_jets/notes/01_COMPLETE_SOURCE_JETS_AND_FIXED_POINT_ENCLOSURES_20261018.md), [code and records](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/05_covariant_theta_jets/numerics/README.md), and [internal review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/05_covariant_theta_jets/reviews/01_COMPLETE_SOURCE_ENCLOSURE_INTERNAL_REVIEW_20261018.md).\n\nThis improves local source evaluation. A benefit for the signed spectral integral, runtime, or exclusion coverage remains unestablished."
